<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
<b>RE: {{{Case.Baggage_File_Reference__c}}}</b>
<p>Thank you for reaching out to the Qantas Customer Care team.<br />
<br />
I'm sorry to hear about recent water damage to your baggage while travelling with us to{{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}}.<br />
<br />
We always take great care when handling customers’ baggage during transfers between&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;and terminals, and we understand how upsetting it can be when personal belongings are damaged.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
<i><strong>Our damaged checked baggage policy&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
<br />
<i><strong>If water damaged occurred due to weather or due to another passenger’s baggage (for example, spillage from another customer’s bag):&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
To assess your claim, please provide clear images showing the damage to your bag and/or its contents, along with receipts for each affected item. If your bag and/or contents can be dry‑cleaned, please also provide receipts for any dry‑cleaning expenses.&nbsp;</p>

<p><i><strong>If the bag or its contents cannot be repaired, restored, or dry‑cleaned, we may offer a replacement bag (Send Delsey replacement email template) or reimbursement for the bag and/or contents, up to the applicable liability limits, subject to receipt and image validation:&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
Thank you for providing the photos and receipts. As the bag and/or items cannot be repaired, restored, or dry‑cleaned,&nbsp;we’re&nbsp;able to offer a replacement Delsey bag and/or reimbursement of AUD$XX for the bag and/or contents, based on the information provided.&nbsp;</p>

<p><i><strong>If the items can be drycleaned, offer drycleaning reimbursement:&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
We’ve&nbsp;got you covered. I understand that you incurred dry-cleaning expenses because of water damage, and&nbsp;I’m&nbsp;happy to review these expenses as part of your claim.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p><i><strong>If images or receipts have not yet been provided or further images are&nbsp;required:</strong></i>&nbsp;<br />
Could you please reply to this email with clear images of the damage, along with your receipts for the affected items' dry‐cleaning expenses. Once received,&nbsp;I’ll&nbsp;review these&nbsp;and action&nbsp;your claim as soon as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>

<p><i><strong>If water damage occurred due to the contents of the passenger’s own bag (for example, a broken bottle of wine or leaking toiletries):&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
I understand your frustration at having damaged baggage. However, in this instance, the damage occurred because of the contents within your own bag. Unfortunately, this means&nbsp;we’re&nbsp;unable to offer compensation on this occasion.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
<i><strong>For Travel insurance requests:&nbsp;</strong></i></p>

<p><i><strong>Insurance letter – damage caused by own contents:&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
Should you&nbsp;require&nbsp;a letter confirming the details of your claim for a third&nbsp;party, for example a travel insurer, we&nbsp;are happy to provide you with one.&nbsp;</p>

<p><i><strong>Insurance letter – proven loss exceeds liability limits:&nbsp;</strong></i><br />
While your damage exceeds the liability limits, we can provide you with a letter confirming the details of your claim.&nbsp;Please let me know if you’d like me to provide you with an insurance letter.</p>
</body>
</html>